          "segmentId": "m00261:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "Diisopropylamine reacts with butyllithium in tetrahydrofuran to form lithium diisopropylamide (known as L D A) and butane. Cyclohexanone reacts with L D A in tetrahydrofuran to form cyclohexanone enolate ion and diisopropylamine."
