    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "table-00001",
      "summary": "An illustration shows the functional groups examples and acidity constants (pKa) for 13 organic compounds. The first functional group is carboxylic acid with an example showing a structure having a methyl group bonded to an acidic group (carbon double bonded to one oxygen atom and bonded to a hydroxyl group with pink hydrogen atom) with pka 5. The second functional group is 1 3-Diketone with an example showing a methyl group bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a methylene group (with pink hydrogens) bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a methyl group with pka 9. The third functional group is 3-Keto ester with an example showing a methyl group bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a pink methylene group (with pink hydrogens) bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a methoxide group with pka 11. The fourth functional group is 1 3-Diester with an example showing a methoxide group bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a methylene group (having pink hydrogens) bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a methoxide group with pka 13. The fifth functional group is Alcohol with an example showing a methyl group bonded to a hydroxy group (having pink hydrogen) with pka 16. The sixth functional group is acid chloride with an example showing a methyl group (having pink hydrogen atoms) bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a chlorine atom with pka 16. The seventh functional group is Aldehyde with an example showing a methyl group (having pink hydrogen atoms) bonded to an aldehyde group with pka 17. The eighth functional group is ketone with an example showing a methyl group (having pink hydrogens) bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a methyl group (having pink hydrogens) with pka 19. The ninth functional group is Thioester with an example showing a methyl group (having pink hydrogens) bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to a sulfur and then a methyl group with pka 21. The tenth functional group is Ester with an example showing a methyl group (having pink hydrogens) bonded to a carbonyl group bonded to methoxide group with pka 25. The eleventh functional group is Nitrile with an example showing a methyl group (having pink hydrogens) bonded to a cyanide group with pka 25. The twelfth functional group is N N-Dialkylamide with an example showing a methyl group (having pink hydrogens) bonded to carbonyl group bonded to a nitrogen bonded to two methyl groups with pka 30. The thirteenth functional group is Dialkylamine with an example showing a pink hydrogen bonded to a nitrogen bonded to two i-C3H7 groups with pka 36.",
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00261:table-title:table-00001-title",
        "text": "Acidity Constants for Some Organic Compounds"
      },
